<section class="sec" id="how" data-od-id="how">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">How it works</span>
      <h2>Three quiet steps. Then it <span class="it">disappears.</span></h2>
      <p>Barakah is not another feed to manage. Set it once and it works in the background, every salah, for as long as you pray.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step reveal">
        <div class="s-num">١</div>
        <h3>Choose what goes quiet</h3>
        <p>Pick the apps that pull at you — social, video, games. Barakah suggests sensible defaults and never touches calls, maps, or Qur'an apps.</p>
        <div class="step-proof">
          <span>Reels</span><span>Shorts</span><span>Games</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step reveal d1">
        <div class="s-num">٢</div>
        <h3>Salah opens, apps close</h3>
        <p>When a prayer window begins, the chosen apps lock for fifteen minutes. A calm screen replaces the feed — a verse, the prayer name, the time.</p>
        <div class="step-proof live">
          <span lang="ar" dir="rtl">حَيَّ عَلَى الصَّلَاةِ</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step reveal d2">
        <div class="s-num">٣</div>
        <h3>Pray, then they return</h3>
        <p>Once you've prayed or the window ends, everything unlocks on its own. No checking in, no streak to defend. Just the day's rhythm, kept.</p>
        <div class="step-proof open">
          <span>Qur'an</span><span>Calls</span><span>Qibla</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
